      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-11-09_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>IROOKE.I BOND &amp; Cot / LTD. MB LANCASIIIRB TBA WARBIIOUSBS 17, PICCADILLY. 1.8&amp;A.N0 tiiiTH 29, MARKET STREET J</head>
        <p>IROOKE.I BOND &amp; Cot / LTD. MB LANCASIIIRB TBA WARBIIOUSBS 17, PICCADILLY. 1.8&amp;A.N0 tiiiTH 29, MARKET STREET J</p>
        <p>• James Floweroft, the under manager, and Isaiah Aldred, ii fireman, entraceri at the Peelwood Pit, belong- ing to the ryldeoley Colliery Company, were drowned In the pit on Saturday night by a sudden inrush of water from an adjolnintr mine. The manager, Mr. G. li.areley, and another fireman, named Doncaster, were also earriei off their feet by the water, but managed to escape with a few brukes.</p>
