      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-11-09_WidnesExaminer_art0087" n="art0087">
        <head>Sutton.</head>
        <p>Sutton.</p>
        <p>REFUSING TO WORK AT TEN WORKISOU•IC.—Two LAZY INHATES.—FFROk Johnson and Robert Prey were charged with being inmates of the workhouse and refusing to perform the tasks allotted them; Joinson was also charged with corn- ! miffing wilful damage to a cell to the extent of 54.—Nr. Curry, the workhouse porter, A dd that on Wednesday morn- ing about 9.30 he was informed that the defendants would not cut any wood. He therefore ordered them to break stones in their cells. Johnson used violent language and broke his cell door with a sledge nammer.—Preee. who pleaded guilty, was committed to goal for one month's hard labour and Johnson for two months.</p>
