      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-11-09_WidnesExaminer_art0088" n="art0088">
        <head>WARRINGTON COUNTY PE rTY SES9ION9.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON COUNTY PE rTY SES9ION9.</p>
        <p>WEDNVIDAY.—BeforP Mr. John Crn.field (chairman). and Mr. J. J. Bleckley.</p>
        <p>DOGS 4T LARGE. - James Houghton was fined ss. ter allow- ing bls dog to be at largeon the 18th Oct. ; James Marsh for two similar offencee was fined 74. 5.1.</p>
        <p>BLACIESMVIIE V. WHEFLRIORT. —A Bcrwrrrtwooo Henry Plerpoint and rilles I:.(srpoint were charged with having on he 10th Oct ,In Burton wood, assaulted and beaten Thomas Dutton —There was a cross-summons oh ,rglng Dut- ton with assaulting the two Pierpoints.—Mr. T. H. Granger appeared for the defendants and Mr. F. R. Roberts for the a mnlainqnt. —Mr Rnberts st•ted that the Property of the parties adjoined, and on the day in question tw; of Mr. Mit- ten's men had set to work to smooth a piece of timber on a road-way close to Mr Piernoint'S land. The latter told the men to remove the timbe-from his I ‘nd and used foul lan- guage. Mr. Dutton hearing thls, came out, and both Pier- points directed their language to him. Mr. Dutton ;ohk an axe and prepared to do the work hint,elt when the defendarts seized it. Henry Pierpoint spat in compl ,inantls five and seized him by the throat threateningly —Thomas Dutton. Thomas Bentley. and Thomas Lse.all corroborated this state• ! ment and denied that the complainant lifted uo the axe to ' strike the 'Plerpeints.—Mr. Gran ,er contended thtt com- plainant attempted to strike the defendants with the axe and denied that the father splt in hi; face.—John le,ster Hill. at. Helens, owner of the land said that the timber had no right to be where complal ;ant put it and (I fendant was right In objecting —The magistrates considered that the question of title of 'And had arisen in the curse of the evi- dence. and therefore, thee had no jurisdiction in the matter. —Both summonses were, therefore. dismissed.</p>
