        <p>.4 [From the Bridgewater MercurY-] 1 --- • wed 41 Mrs. WEST, Bath-road, Bridgewater, was instated 12 tervie . • , by a" Bridgewater Mercury " reporter, and reply to questions, the facts of an extraordinarY afftLit.;',ll the reports of which had led the interviewer to , 1) • himself '</p>
        <p>The reporter adds that he could hardly brinl - to imagine that the clear countenance of the Perso°,ll9°°„as whom he gazed was, not long ago, disfigured and blind. Mrs. Mrs. West said, six yearsiago, eruptions began to pear on her chin, and gradually extended up to thole° side of her face, afterwards spreading to the right eide• The eruptions were accompanied by severe and she became almost blind. When her faco beesa 0 get bad she went to the Bridgewater Infirmary, but bet face gradually got worse. She consulted doctors, 1:113V with the same effect ; used pills, ointment, and yaedr: cated soap, but no good resulted, and her face still corto tinned to get worse. She could hardly hear to touch if, it was so sore and swollen, and when in the cold suffering was terrible. - Her general health also got ba° • swellingS. and she lost her appetite. And M. West significaner added,' If I had continued I should have been In the cemetery before now." Asked how she accounted for the great charge...KV:: her condition, which enabled her to shun the cernete'r, Mrs. West replied that nearly two years ago she Barr Dr:" Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People mentioned in a 1000 paper as a remedy for disorders arising from impofet" ' ished blood ,and she was advised to try them by P0111•,' who were able to testify to their great efficacy. "Alca°9 as soon as I began to take them," she added, " MY face' commenced to get better." went Mrs. West went on to say that the swellings - - down, the eruptions began to disappear, and she vraill soon able to see again all right, and her health all/C ./2'l' rapidly improved. As the pills did her so much g°°;, : she had continued to take a box of them every since she first tried them, and her face had now 4008 ' got well. Dr. Williams' Piak Pills enrich the blood, and ; cure skin troubles and blood disardere, also Part lirtV locomator ataxy, neuralgia, rheumatism, Sr. ea dance, nervous headache, and indigestion ; e, rester the blood,such as sc